# SkillBridge workflow orchestrator

`skillbridge/orchestrator.py` is deterministic workflow infrastructure, not a fourth
specialized AI agent. It sends versioned `AgentRequestMessage` messages to the three
specialized agents using the installed uAgents `Context.send_and_receive` API.
`agents/orchestrator_agent.py` is the separate standalone Agentverse deployment for
users who want to chat through Agent Chat Protocol; it gathers explicit candidate
details with ASI:One and coordinates those same three agents.

Configure the three deployed agent addresses before starting the orchestrator:

```text
SKILLBRIDGE_OPPORTUNITY_AGENT_ADDRESS=<uAgents address>
SKILLBRIDGE_EVIDENCE_AGENT_ADDRESS=<uAgents address>
SKILLBRIDGE_ACTION_AGENT_ADDRESS=<uAgents address>
```

Optional workflow settings:

```text
SKILLBRIDGE_WORKFLOW_TIMEOUT=30
SKILLBRIDGE_WORKFLOW_MAX_ATTEMPTS=2
SKILLBRIDGE_WORKFLOW_DB=skillbridge_workflows.sqlite3
SKILLBRIDGE_ORCHESTRATOR_SEED=<private deployment seed>
SKILLBRIDGE_ORCHESTRATOR_PORT=8000
```

Agent addresses must be distinct valid uAgents addresses. The messages use
uAgents' signed-agent transport; the incoming workflow handler does not allow
unverified messages. Keep seeds and credentials in the deployment environment,
not in this repository.

An API/client sends an `AgentRequest` with `recipient="orchestrator"`,
`message_type="candidate.workflow.run"`, a unique `request_id`, and a payload
matching `CandidateWorkflowRequest`. The payload contains the candidate,
`job_search` (`OpportunitySearchRequest`), declared skills, assessment,
practical-task and project records, `as_of`, and optional matching/action
configuration. The orchestrator evaluates candidate evidence independently of
job search and runs those two requests concurrently. It forwards only validated
results and optional measured improvement metadata to the Career Action Agent.

Start it from the repository root with `python -m skillbridge.orchestrator`
after installing the dependencies and setting the required addresses.

Completed workflows are stored in SQLite with the job provenance and retrieval
times, evidence profile and references, matching rubric, and action plan. The
request body itself and credentials are not stored. Reusing the same request ID
with the same input returns the cached result with `replayed=true`; reusing it
with different input is rejected. Partial job-source failures remain labeled
and are preserved in the workflow response.

Configure the Opportunity Agent separately with `JOB_SOURCE=remotive` for live
job data, or `SKILLBRIDGE_USE_FIXTURES=1` for clearly labeled development
fixtures. The orchestrator never substitutes fixtures.

Provider HTTP calls default to a 10-second connection timeout and a 60-second
response data idle timeout. The idle timer applies between incoming data reads,
not to the total response duration, so a slow but active transfer can continue;
a response that stops sending data times out after 60 seconds.

## Agentverse conversational orchestrator

Deploy `agents/orchestrator_agent.py` as a fourth hosted uAgent (the coordinator,
not a fourth specialized AI agent). It registers Agent Chat Protocol handlers and
uses ASI:One to extract only facts from the current user message. It asks for
missing role, country, experience, learning availability, and location details;
it then sends versioned requests to the Opportunity Intelligence, Candidate
Evidence, and Career Action agents. Job matching and recommendations remain
deterministic in the specialized agents. It does not cache prior recommendations
as fresh results or replace failed live calls with fixtures.

Configure these environment values/secrets on the hosted orchestrator:

```text
ASI1_API_KEY=<ASI:One API key secret>
SKILLBRIDGE_OPPORTUNITY_AGENT_ADDRESS=<deployed Opportunity agent address>
SKILLBRIDGE_EVIDENCE_AGENT_ADDRESS=<deployed Candidate Evidence agent address>
SKILLBRIDGE_ACTION_AGENT_ADDRESS=<deployed Career Action agent address>
```

Optional ASI:One settings are `ASI1_BASE_URL` (defaults to
`https://api.asi1.ai/v1`) and `SKILLBRIDGE_LLM_MODEL` (defaults to `asi1`).
`ASI_ONE_API_KEY` is accepted as a local-development compatibility fallback;
use Agentverse's `ASI1_API_KEY` secret for hosted deployment. The three addresses
must be distinct valid uAgents addresses and refer to deployed, reachable agents.
Configure the Opportunity agent itself with `JOB_SOURCE=remotive` for live jobs;
configure each hosted agent's own seed through its deployment settings, never in
source code. No API key is required for Remotive.

Career guidance can use a compact summary of required and preferred skills from
up to ten validated job listings, so suggestions can reflect custom roles
returned by Remotive without forwarding entire job descriptions. This is a
market signal, not proof that a certification is required by an employer.

Certification suggestions are restricted to credentials relevant to the role
and to the issuer-reference catalog in `agents/action_agent.py`. The catalog
contains reviewed requirement summaries for selected CompTIA, AWS, Google
Cloud, and Microsoft credentials; entries without a reviewed summary link to the
official issuer page and are explicitly labeled as not verified. The summaries
are snapshots, not a live issuer feed: review `CERTIFICATION_REQUIREMENTS_CHECKED_ON`
and refresh them against the linked issuer pages before deployment updates.
Identical guidance requests are cached in-process for one hour, scoped by model,
role, location, candidate context, job signals, and requested topics.